{"w":2400,"h":3209,"lines":[{"y":0.082452148763372257,"w":0.13611609141031894,"t":"READING","x":0.41932059499441893,"h":0.019688725694317677,"c":1},{"h":0.017515213987166267,"c":1,"t":"READING PASSAGE 1","x":0.069902915115357581,"y":0.14672897199547363,"w":0.30679611206054691},{"h":0.019042056074766278,"c":1,"t":"You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 1-13, which are based on Reading","y":0.18750000027403457,"x":0.06990290906543066,"w":0.81165049235026043},{"h":0.019533165667287244,"y":0.20528037970372837,"w":0.16946029663085938,"c":1,"x":0.069599657156504929,"t":"Passage 1 below."},{"c":1,"x":0.40351347721473568,"y":0.24526466775047329,"w":0.16768381754557288,"t":"Stonehenge","h":0.021887905798225749},{"x":0.069902901904562595,"w":0.77864079793294272,"y":0.28779069756162401,"t":"For centuries, historians and archaeologists have puzzled over the many mysteries","h":0.017505252398434479,"c":1},{"c":0.30000001192092896,"x":0.083333324564360295,"y":0.30404984422317316,"t":"f satedhen saisbury hisain in soutment ingland tas esimated o froughys to massive","w":0.80555557250976562,"h":0.037694704049844319},{"y":0.3429906540873795,"t":"upright stones placed in a circular layout.","w":0.39223302205403648,"h":0.019003115264797588,"x":0.067961158740129882,"c":1},{"t":"Archaeologists believe England's most iconic prehistoric ruin was built in several stages,","x":0.069902919677958739,"c":1,"h":0.017570455794765238,"y":0.38068535826707883,"w":0.83300969441731787},{"t":"with the earliest constructed 5,000 or more years ago. First, Neolithic* Britons used","y":0.39788981333854145,"h":0.022242494387047285,"c":1,"x":0.069840390747307968,"w":0.77879272460937499},{"t":"primitive tools, which may have been fashioned out of deer antlers, to dig a massive","c":1,"h":0.017532420529754678,"w":0.78834950764973954,"x":0.069902915980202915,"y":0.41860465104999034},{"c":1,"y":0.43600626597232295,"x":0.069858812293491238,"t":"circular ditch and bank, or henge. Deep pits dating back to that era and located within","h":0.019349278245016865,"w":0.80203124999999997},{"h":0.017450916729983557,"w":0.76699030558268233,"x":0.067961157786250795,"y":0.45638629268055708,"t":"the circle may have once held a ring of timber posts, according to some scholars.","c":1},{"w":0.80403625488281261,"t":"Several hundred years later, it is thought, Stonehenge's builders hoisted an estimated","c":1,"y":0.49040251009251357,"x":0.069834728848630429,"h":0.022356410041405095},{"h":0.017543287663444929,"c":1,"y":0.51152647988677125,"t":"80 bluestones, 43 of which remain today, into standing positions and placed them in","x":0.069902908078744677,"w":0.78640777587890631},{"w":0.78465891520182285,"y":0.52770058664980701,"c":1,"t":"either a horseshoe or circular formation. These stones have been traced all the way","x":0.069820853225328869,"h":0.020448084560881541},{"t":"to the Preseli Hills in Wales, some 300 kilometres from Stonehenge. How, then, did","w":0.78058252970377606,"h":0.019013076853529265,"x":0.067961162237648129,"y":0.54796511655193791,"c":1},{"x":0.069858106811964263,"w":0.83309717814127604,"c":1,"y":0.56589770334538814,"h":0.019995613930010037,"t":"prehistoric builders without sophisticated tools or engineering haul these boulders, which"},{"t":"weigh up to four tons, over such a great distance?","y":0.5856697821069593,"h":0.019003115264797477,"x":0.069902925121160517,"c":1,"w":0.47184463500976564},{"w":0.79427154541015632,"t":"According to one long-standing theory among archaeologists, Stonehenge's builders","x":0.067917389733742742,"y":0.62188483382527771,"h":0.020324249505253911,"c":1},{"c":1,"x":0.06796117285221176,"y":0.64236760111980029,"t":"fashioned sledges and rollers out of tree trunks to lug the bluestones from the Preseli","w":0.80194173177083328,"h":0.016199376947040545},{"t":"Hills. They then transferred the boulders onto rafts and floated them first along the","w":0.76893203735351567,"x":0.069902918488290694,"y":0.65981308397918592,"c":1,"h":0.017512497352291101},{"x":0.069778600977778729,"h":0.02276281790569934,"w":0.81576492309570314,"c":1,"y":0.67550624212937627,"t":"Welsh coast and then up the River Avon toward Salisbury Plain; alternatively, they may"},{"x":0.067961161534052322,"y":0.69767441849077561,"w":0.81165049235026043,"h":0.017590378972228815,"t":"have towed each stone with a fleet of vessels. More recent archaeological hypotheses","c":1},{"c":1,"t":"have them transporting the bluestones with supersized wicker baskets on a combination","x":0.067961173837714828,"y":0.71651090354921632,"w":0.82718444824218751,"h":0.016199376947040545},{"c":1,"x":0.069902920165711174,"y":0.73546511616485866,"t":"of ball bearings and long grooved planks, hauled by oxen.","w":0.54563105265299472,"h":0.017494385264744228},{"w":0.77864079793294261,"y":0.77165109054591718,"x":0.069902901952712385,"h":0.017593095607103981,"t":"As early as the 1970s, geologists have been adding their voices to the debate over","c":1},{"t":"how Stonehenge came into being. Challenging the classic image of industrious builders","x":0.06990292314351601,"w":0.82135920206705737,"h":0.017485329220970902,"y":0.79065420577101397,"c":1},{"c":1,"y":0.80798879015790204,"x":0.067910990916884947,"h":0.021877614434262949,"t":"pushing, carting, rolling or hauling giant stones from faraway Wales, some scientists","w":0.79039637247721373},{"w":0.835065409342448,"h":0.021425206787489715,"x":0.067920995859780744,"y":0.82737591725525195,"c":1,"t":"have suggested that it was glaciers, not humans, that carried the bluestones to Salisbury"},{"y":0.84370529972045016,"c":1,"h":0.023075419868635594,"t":"Plain. Most archaeologists have remained sceptical about this theory, however,","x":0.069790510220591864,"w":0.74392908732096352},{"h":0.015988371899566145,"w":0.81165049235026043,"t":"wondering how the forces of nature could possibly have delivered the exact number of","x":0.067961161500166442,"y":0.86627906986215175,"c":1},{"h":0.017525175575898055,"w":0.35533978780110675,"c":1,"x":0.067961177288766952,"t":"stones needed to complete the circle.","y":0.88372093049817757},{"h":0.014326119348638811,"c":1,"y":0.92731041129936265,"t":"* Neolithic - The era, also known as the New Stone Age, which began around 12,000 years ago and ended around 3500 BCE","w":0.75152664184570317,"x":0.06792133683144129},{"w":0.02718446731567381,"y":0.95348837196339387,"h":0.01308139551465759,"c":1,"t":"39","x":0.87572815459459019}]}